(244337, 15687, 6870, '<td valign="top">This fine image would be even better if it were larger. Your lighting and composition are great. If you use Photoshop, you can go to your Image Size... window and adjust the dpi. The max for use here is 640 for your longest edges. You can then use the "Save for Web..." window and fiddle there until you have a jpg image that is under 150 kb. Good luck.</td>', 'This fine image would be even better if it were larger. Your lighting and composition are great. If you use Photoshop, you can go to your Image Size... window and adjust the dpi. The max for use here is 640 for your longest edges. You can then use the "Save for Web..." window and fiddle there until you have a jpg image that is under 150 kb. Good luck.', '2003-03-24 09:35:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(244342, 15761, 7364, '<td valign="top">Composition seems unbalanced, boy''s face needs more dimension.  Excellent dimension in man''s face.  Why is the man looking down or have his eyes shut when the boy is looking at th camera?  It gives each subject a different relationship to the viewer.  Is the man reading him a book?  is he asleep?  These are the questions that run through my mind.</td>', 'Composition seems unbalanced, boy''s face needs more dimension.  Excellent dimension in man''s face.  Why is the man looking down or have his eyes shut when the boy is looking at th camera?  It gives each subject a different relationship to the viewer.  Is the man reading him a book?  is he asleep?  These are the questions that run through my mind.', '2003-03-24 09:40:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(244350, 15977, 7364, '<td valign="top">Are you sure this wan''t taken 60 years ago?  It looks great!  My only suggestion would be to add some more color to the photo, or take more out.  We''re in a washe dout midde ground that doens''t seem to be intentional - especially notided in the green of the trees.  Just a thought, I wonder what thsi pic would look like in b/w or sepia.  BTW, are those potty sheds in the background?</td>', 'Are you sure this wan''t taken 60 years ago?  It looks great!  My only suggestion would be to add some more color to the photo, or take more out.  We''re in a washe dout midde ground that doens''t seem to be intentional - especially notided in the green of the trees.  Just a thought, I wonder what thsi pic would look like in b/w or sepia.  BTW, are those potty sheds in the background?', '2003-03-24 09:57:26.000000', NULL, 1),
